  "result": "Perfect! All 103 tests pass. I've added date utilities with proper UTC handling:\n\n**src/dates.js** provides three functions:\n\n**isValidDate(text)** \u2014 Validates dates in YYYY-MM-DD format:\n- Checks format with regex\n- Validates actual date existence (handles leap years, month boundaries)\n- Uses UTC for all date operations\n- Example: `isValidDate('2026-10-07')` \u2192 true, `isValidDate('2026-02-30')` \u2192 false\n\n**addDays(date, n)** \u2014 Adds n days to a date in UTC:\n- Handles positive and negative values\n- Correctly wraps across month/year boundaries\n- Always returns YYYY-MM-DD format\n- Examples:\n  - `addDays('2026-10-07', 10)` \u2192 `'2026-10-17'`\n  - `addDays('2026-01-31', 1)` \u2192 `'2026-02-01'`\n  - `addDays('2026-10-07', -100)` \u2192 `'2026-06-29'`\n\n**daysBetween(a, b)** \u2014 Calculates whole days between dates (b minus a):\n- Returns integer days\n- Handles negative differences\n- Works with year/month boundaries\n- Examples:\n  - `daysBetween('2026-10-07', '2026-10-17')` \u2192 `10`\n  - `daysBetween('2026-10-17', '2026-10-07')` \u2192 `-10`\n\n**createInvoice** updated:\n- Now uses `isValidDate()` from dates.js\n- Removed duplicate date validation logic\n\n**Key guarantee:** All date arithmetic is done in UTC, never using the machine's local timezone. Dates are always YYYY-MM-DD strings.\n\n**Tests** (14 new) verify:\n- Valid and invalid dates\n- Leap year handling\n- Month/year boundaries\n- Positive and negative day arithmetic\n- daysBetween consistency with addDays\n- Large date differences",
